{"name":"Pictorial Carmine","hex":"#c30b4e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pictorial","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, composed of, or illustrated by pictures.","Described or otherwise represented as if in a picture; graphic or vivid."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A newspaper or magazine with many pictures, or section thereof.","An article primarily featuring many photographs, or simply a collection of photographs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pictorial"},{"term":"carmine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A purplish-red pigment, made from dye obtained from the cochineal beetle; carminic acid or any of its derivatives.","A purplish-red colour, resembling that pigment."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the purplish red colour shade carmine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carmine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Image","blocks":[{"text":"An image or picture is a visual representation. An image can be two-dimensional, such as a drawing, painting, or photograph, or three-dimensional, such as a carving or sculpture. Images may be displayed through other media, including a projection on a surface, activation of electronic signals, or digital displays; they can also be reproduced through mechanical means, such as photography, printmaking, or photocopying. Images can also be animated through digital or physical processes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Image_created_with_a_mobile_phone.png/330px-Image_created_with_a_mobile_phone.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image"},{"title":"Carmine","blocks":[{"text":"Carmine – also called cochineal, cochineal extract, crimson lake, or carmine lake – is a pigment of a bright-red color obtained from the aluminium complex derived from carminic acid. Specific code names for the pigment include natural red 4, C.I. 75470, or E120. Carmine is also a general term for a particularly deep-red color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Carmine.svg/330px-Carmine.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmine"},{"title":"Carmine (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Carmine color is the general term for some deep red colors that are very slightly purplish but are generally slightly closer to pure red than the color crimson is. Some rubies have the color shown below as rich carmine. The deep dark red color shown at right as carmine is the color of the raw unprocessed pigment, but lighter, richer, or brighter colors are produced when the raw pigment is processed, some of which are shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Carmine.png/330px-Carmine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmine_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/TEIDE.JPG/500px-TEIDE.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/TEIDE.JPG/1280px-TEIDE.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/TEIDE.JPG/500px-TEIDE.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A synthetic aperture radar image acquired by the SIR-C/X-SAR radar on board the Space Shuttle Endeavour shows the Teide volcano. The city of Santa Cruz de Tenerife is visible as the purple and white area on the lower right edge of the island. Lava flows at the summit crater appear in shades of green and brown, while vegetation zones appear as areas of purple, green, and yellow on the volcano's flanks.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATEIDE.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb